  "title": "Subsidised drought insurance for farmers in Austria",
  "summary": "The subsidised public-private drought insurance system for agriculture adopted by the Austrian government combines indemnity-based insurance with weather index-based products. It aims at preparing farmers to overcome extreme events, reduce their dependence on subsidies and as such promote their well-being and mental health, while simultaneously allowing through public-private partnerships for better financial planning. Agriculture is highly sensitive to weather extremes, such as droughts, floods, storms, hail and heat. Drought in particular poses a significant challenge to farmers and governments due to its potential, negative impact on crop yields.",
